{"description": "Calls a manifested Prompt Builder prompt once per chunk and stores what it returns as the chunk's context header and as its own columns on the chunk table, so the embedding sees a chunk that says where it came from. Chain the step to run several prompts, one after the other.", "displayName": "RAG - Enrich Chunks.step", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [{"name": "_rgen_inventory", "displayName": "_rgen_inventory", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "type": "table", "id": "_rgen_inventory", "label": "_rgen_inventory"}], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgen_invout", "displayName": "_rgen_invout", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "columnDelta": null, "type": "table"}]}, "metadataVersion": 1, "name": "RAG - Enrich Chunks.step", "properties": {}, "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - Enrich Chunks: call a manifested Prompt Builder prompt once per chunk\n * in <project>_CHUNKS and write what it returns back into the same table -\n * the chosen output as the chunk's context header, the others as their own\n * columns. The Embed step then prepends that header before embedding, which\n * is the whole point of the stage. Thin shell over rag_core.enrich.run_enrich\n * - see the About tab.\n *\n * The step may appear MORE THAN ONCE in a flow, to run several prompts one\n * after the other. Each one adds to what the last wrote: the chunk's\n * attributes merge, enrich_version records every prompt that contributed, and\n * the usage tally accumulates so the Load step still creates every column.\n * Only one of them may write the context header - a chunk has one.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgen_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgen_ragProject) %then %global _rgen_ragProject;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgen_tablesCaslib) %then %global _rgen_tablesCaslib;\n%mend _rgen_setup;\n%_rgen_setup;\n/* Pipeline-wide state, shared by every RAG step in this session.\n   RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR: 1 (default) stops a SAS Studio Flow at the failing\n   step, which is what an interactive user wants. A SCHEDULED run sets it to\n   0: an aborted session never sends SAS Job Execution its completion\n   handshake, so the job would report running forever and its dead compute\n   server would keep counting against the context's server limit.\n   RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED: set by the step that fails; later steps then skip\n   their work and pass the inventory through, so the flow finishes tidily\n   instead of loading half a corpus. */\n%macro _rag_pipeline_state;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR) %then %do;\n        %global RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR;\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED) %then %global RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rag_pipeline_state;\n%_rag_pipeline_state;\n\n%let _rgen_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgen_rc = 1;\n%let _rgen_state = run;\n%let _rgen_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgen_summary = ;\n%let _rgen_nrows = 0;\n%let _rgen_ninv = 0;\n/* <project>_CHUNKS is the Chunk step's table; this step rewrites it in place,\n   so it has to persist it the same way or a restart would resurrect the\n   unenriched generation from the saved file. */\n%macro _rgen_persist_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgen_persist) %then %global _rgen_persist;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgen_persist)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgen_persist = 1;\n%mend _rgen_persist_default;\n%_rgen_persist_default;\n\n%macro _rgen_guard;\n    %if &RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED. NE 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgen_state = skip;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Enrich Chunks: skipped - an earlier step of this run failed\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgen_guard;\n%_rgen_guard;\n%macro _rgen_inherit;\n    %global _rgen_runId;\n    %local dsid vproject vcaslib vrun rc;\n    %if %symexist(_rgen_inventory) %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgen_inventory)) NE 0 %then %do;\n        %if %sysfunc(exist(&_rgen_inventory.)) %then %do;\n            %let dsid = %sysfunc(open(&_rgen_inventory., i));\n            %if &dsid. NE 0 %then %do;\n                %let vproject = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., rag_project));\n                %let vcaslib = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., tables_caslib));\n                %let vrun = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., run_id));\n                %if %sysfunc(fetch(&dsid.)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n                    %if &vproject. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgen_ragProject = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vproject.));\n                    %if &vcaslib. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgen_tablesCaslib = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vcaslib.));\n                    /* the run id too: the lock belongs to the RUN, so a step\n                       that fails has to know which lock row to hand back */\n                    %if &vrun. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgen_runId = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vrun.));\n                %end;\n                %let rc = %sysfunc(close(&dsid.));\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n    /* a missing project is a failure of THIS step - but not when the step is\n       already skipping, where an absent inventory is expected */\n    %if &_rgen_state. EQ run %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgen_ragProject)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgen_state = fail;\n        /* one line: the value is embedded in a quoted putLog below, so a\n           newline inside it would break the string */\n        %let _rgen_error = the inventory does not name a RAG project - wire the output of RAG - List Documents into this step;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgen_tablesCaslib)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgen_tablesCaslib = casuser;\n%mend _rgen_inherit;\n%_rgen_inherit;\n%macro _rgen_port_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgen_invout) %then %global _rgen_invout;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgen_invout)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgen_invout = rgenout.&_rgen_ragProject._INV_EMBED;\n%mend _rgen_port_default;\n%_rgen_port_default;\n/* One CAS session for the whole step: created here, reused by\n   SWAT inside proc python, promote+save done by proc casutil.\n   rgenout is where the step's OUTPUT TABLE lands by default -\n   the same caslib as the pipeline tables, so a flow leaves its\n   intermediate results next to each other. */\ncas rgencas uuidmac=_rgen_casuuid;\n%let _rgen_cashost = %sysfunc(getoption(CASHOST));\n%let _rgen_casport = %sysfunc(getoption(CASPORT));\nlibname rgenout cas caslib=\"&_rgen_tablesCaslib.\" sessref=rgencas;\n\n%macro _rgen_export(portvar, file);\n    %if %symexist(&portvar.) %then %do;\n        %if %length(%superq(&&portvar.)) GT 0 %then %do;\n            %if %sysfunc(exist(&&&portvar..)) %then %do;\n                filename _rgen_io \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/&file.\";\n                proc json out=_rgen_io noSASTags;\n                    export &&&portvar..;\n                run; quit;\n                filename _rgen_io clear;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgen_export;\n%_rgen_export(_rgen_inventory, rgen_inventory_in.json);\n\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    # nothing to do when the step is only passing the inventory through\n    if str(SAS.symget(\"_rgen_state\") or \"run\").strip() != \"run\":\n        return\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for ch in (\"'\", '\"', \"%\", \"&\", \";\"):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(ch, \" \")\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGENRICH \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgen_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import swat\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgen_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the swat/pandas packages \"\n                                   \"required for the CAS table transport - \"\n                                   \"see the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgen_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgen_promptModel\",\n        \"_rgen_promptVersion\",\n        \"_rgen_mapping\",\n        \"_rgen_headerOutput\",\n        \"_rgen_columns\",\n        \"_rgen_workers\",\n        \"_rgen_ragProject\",\n        \"_rgen_tablesCaslib\",\n        \"_rgen_ragCorePath\",\n        \"_rgen_credentialDomain\",\n    ]}\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def multiline(control):\n        \"\"\"Every line a user typed into a multi-line text field.\n\n        SAS Studio splits such a field for us: it emits <control>_count and\n        <control>_1..N, and leaves the plain macro variable holding only the\n        FIRST line. Reading just the plain one silently turned two questions\n        into one run-on question (found live in a flow). Semicolons are still\n        accepted, for callers that set the parameter directly.\n        \"\"\"\n        values = []\n        try:\n            count = int(float(SAS.symget(control + \"_count\") or 0))\n        except Exception:\n            count = 0\n        if count > 0:\n            for index in range(1, count + 1):\n                try:\n                    piece = str(SAS.symget(\"%s_%d\" % (control, index)) or \"\")\n                except Exception:\n                    piece = \"\"\n                if piece.strip():\n                    values.append(piece.strip())\n            if values:\n                return values\n        raw = str(P.get(control) or \"\").replace(\";\", \"\\n\")\n        return [line.strip() for line in raw.split(\"\\n\") if line.strip()]\n\n    def clean_path(raw):\n        \"\"\"Path-selector values arrive scheme-prefixed (sasserver:/...,\n        sascontent:/...); strip the scheme off.\"\"\"\n        value = str(raw or \"\").strip()\n        for scheme in (\"sascontent:\", \"sasserver:\"):\n            if value.lower().startswith(scheme):\n                return value[len(scheme):]\n        return value\n\n    STARTED = time.time()\n    SUMMARY = []\n\n    def summarize(line):\n        \"\"\"One line of the step's log summary (SAS prints them at the end).\"\"\"\n        SUMMARY.append(str(line))\n\n    def publish_summary(target):\n        elapsed = time.time() - STARTED\n        summarize(f\"elapsed {elapsed:.1f}s\")\n        SAS.symput(target, sas_safe(\" | \".join(SUMMARY))[:1500])\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    try:\n        # ---- CAS: reuse the session the step created in SAS ---------------\n        # (sas-studio-custom-steps: Reuse-CAS-session-from-SWAT)\n        import re as _re\n        os.environ.setdefault(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\",\n                              os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\", \"\"))\n        try:\n            conn = swat.CAS(hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgen_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                            port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgen_casport\") or 5570)),\n                            password=TOKEN,\n                            session=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgen_casuuid\") or \"\"))\n        except Exception as exc:\n            # The step reuses the CAS session SAS created, because the staged\n            # table has to be visible to the casutil promote that follows. CAS\n            # only lets an identity reconnect to its OWN session, and a context\n            # that runs the server as a service account breaks that: SAS and\n            # its token are the service account while the CAS session belongs\n            # to the user who launched the job.\n            #\n            # SWAT's exception says only \"Could not connect ... on port 5570\";\n            # the server's real message (\"Users can only reconnect to their own\n            # sessions\") goes to stderr and never reaches the exception, so\n            # matching on text does not work. Connecting WITHOUT the session id\n            # separates the two causes: if that works, CAS is reachable and the\n            # problem is whose session it is.\n            reachable = False\n            try:\n                probe = swat.CAS(\n                    hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgen_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                    port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgen_casport\") or 5570)),\n                    password=TOKEN)\n                reachable = True\n                probe.close()\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            if reachable:\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    \"this compute context cannot run the RAG steps: CAS is \"\n                    \"reachable, but the SAS session and the CAS session belong \"\n                    \"to different identities, so the step cannot reuse the CAS \"\n                    \"session it needs. The stock 'SAS Job Execution compute \"\n                    \"context' has this problem because it runs the server as a \"\n                    \"service account. Run the job in a context that runs as the \"\n                    \"REQUESTING USER - the 'SAS Studio compute context' does, \"\n                    \"and a full flow was verified there. See the RAG \"\n                    \"administration guide.\")\n            raise\n        CASLIB = P[\"_rgen_tablesCaslib\"] or \"casuser\"\n        if not _re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,19}$\",\n                         P[\"_rgen_ragProject\"] or \"\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"ragProject must be 1-20 characters (letters, digits, \"\n                \"underscores, starting with a letter) so every \"\n                \"project_suffix table name stays within the 32 characters \"\n                \"SAS Studio displays\")\n\n        def project_table(suffix):\n            return P[\"_rgen_ragProject\"] + suffix\n\n        def stamp(rows):\n            \"\"\"Every inventory row names its pipeline, so the next step\n            inherits the project and caslib instead of asking again.\"\"\"\n            for row in rows:\n                row[\"rag_project\"] = P[\"_rgen_ragProject\"]\n                row[\"tables_caslib\"] = CASLIB\n            return rows\n\n        def cas_read(name, required_message=None):\n            \"\"\"Read a pipeline table into lower-cased row dicts; absent\n            table = empty (the pipeline's empty state) unless required.\"\"\"\n            if not conn.table.tableExists(caslib=CASLIB, name=name).exists:\n                if required_message:\n                    raise RuntimeError(required_message)\n                return []\n            frame = conn.CASTable(name, caslib=CASLIB).to_frame()\n            rows = []\n            for record in frame.to_dict(\"records\"):\n                row = {}\n                for key, value in record.items():\n                    row[str(key).lower()] = None if pd.isna(value) else value\n                rows.append(row)\n            return rows\n\n        def label_columns(name, columns):\n            \"\"\"Put the shipped column labels on a CAS table - they survive\n            the promote, so the pipeline tables read without the schema.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                from rag_core.steps import column_labels\n                labels = column_labels(columns)\n                if labels:\n                    conn.table.alterTable(\n                        caslib=CASLIB, name=name,\n                        columns=[{\"name\": column, \"label\": label}\n                                 for column, label in labels.items()])\n            except Exception as exc:\n                M(f\"column labels not applied to {name}: {exc}\")\n\n        def cas_stage(name, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n            \"\"\"Upload the session-scope staging table <name>_S with varchar\n            columns (no 32k limit); the SAS side swaps it into the promoted\n            global table and saves it, so the previous state survives a\n            mid-step failure.\"\"\"\n            if not rows:\n                return 0\n            data = []\n            for row in rows:\n                rec = []\n                for column in columns:\n                    value = row.get(column)\n                    if column in numeric:\n                        try:\n                            rec.append(float(value or 0))\n                        except Exception:\n                            rec.append(0.0)\n                    else:\n                        rec.append(\"\" if value is None else str(value))\n                data.append(rec)\n            frame = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=list(columns))\n            spec = [{\"name\": column,\n                     \"type\": \"double\" if column in numeric else \"varchar\"}\n                    for column in columns]\n            conn.upload_frame(frame,\n                              casout={\"name\": name + \"_S\", \"caslib\": CASLIB,\n                                      \"replace\": True},\n                              importoptions={\"fileType\": \"csv\",\n                                             \"allowEmbeddedNewLines\": True,\n                                             \"vars\": spec})\n            label_columns(name + \"_S\", columns)\n            return len(rows)\n\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = (clean_path(P[\"_rgen_ragCorePath\"])\n                     or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\")\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        def chunk_to_row(chunk):\n            row = dict(chunk)\n            for column in (\"span\", \"tags\", \"attributes\", \"entities\",\n                           \"relations\", \"embedding\"):\n                value = chunk.get(column)\n                row[column] = json.dumps(value) if value not in (None, \"\", {}) else \"\"\n            return row\n\n        def row_to_chunk(row):\n            chunk = dict(row)\n            chunk[\"chunk_index\"] = int(float(row.get(\"chunk_index\") or 0))\n            for column in (\"span\", \"entities\", \"relations\", \"embedding\"):\n                chunk[column] = json.loads(row[column]) if row.get(column) else None\n            chunk[\"attributes\"] = (json.loads(row[\"attributes\"])\n                                   if row.get(\"attributes\") else {})\n            chunk[\"tags\"] = json.loads(row[\"tags\"]) if row.get(\"tags\") else {}\n            for column in (\"heading_path\", \"prev_id\", \"next_id\", \"context_header\"):\n                chunk[column] = row.get(column) or None\n            return chunk\n\n        from rag_core.credentials import fetch_secrets\n        from rag_core.enrich import (PromptModel, attribute_schema,\n                                     parse_mapping, parse_names, run_enrich,\n                                     validate_selection)\n        from rag_core.pricing import log_enrich_cost\n        from rag_core.providers import llm_api_key_for\n        from rag_core.steps import (CHUNK_COLUMNS, INVENTORY_COLUMNS,\n                                    stamp_enrich_usage)\n\n        inventory_columns = INVENTORY_COLUMNS\n        inventory = read_rows(\"rgen_inventory_in.json\",\n                              \"the inventory input port is not connected - \"\n                              \"wire the RAG - Chunk Documents \"\n                              \"updated-inventory output into this step\")\n        model_id = P[\"_rgen_promptModel\"]\n        mapping = parse_mapping(P[\"_rgen_mapping\"])\n        header_output = P[\"_rgen_headerOutput\"]\n        column_outputs = parse_names(P[\"_rgen_columns\"])\n        chunks = [row_to_chunk(row)\n                  for row in cas_read(project_table(\"_CHUNKS\"))]\n\n        if not model_id:\n            # No prompt: the stage is configured off. The chunk table is left\n            # exactly as the Chunk step wrote it - NOT rewritten with empty\n            # headers, which would retire a generation for nothing.\n            n_inventory = write_rows(\"rgen_inventory_out.json\", stamp(inventory),\n                                     inventory_columns, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n            SAS.symput(\"_rgen_ninv\", str(n_inventory))\n            SAS.symput(\"_rgen_nrows\", \"-1\")\n            summarize(\"no prompt model set - chunks pass through unenriched\")\n            publish_summary(\"_rgen_summary\")\n        elif not chunks:\n            stamp_enrich_usage(inventory, {})\n            n_inventory = write_rows(\"rgen_inventory_out.json\", stamp(inventory),\n                                     inventory_columns, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n            SAS.symput(\"_rgen_ninv\", str(n_inventory))\n            SAS.symput(\"_rgen_nrows\", \"-1\")\n            summarize(\"no chunks pending - nothing to enrich\")\n            publish_summary(\"_rgen_summary\")\n        else:\n            # The prompt is loaded and checked BEFORE anything is called: a\n            # mapping that names an input this prompt does not have is a\n            # five-second failure here, and a per-chunk failure otherwise.\n            # A blank version follows the model; a version id pins this\n            # setup to exactly the prompt that version carried.\n            prompt = PromptModel.from_model_manager(\n                BASE, TOKEN, model_id,\n                version_id=P[\"_rgen_promptVersion\"], verify=VERIFY)\n            M(\"enrich prompt: \" + prompt.describe()\n              + (\" [pinned]\" if P[\"_rgen_promptVersion\"] else \" [latest]\"))\n            problems = validate_selection(prompt, mapping, header_output,\n                                          column_outputs)\n            if problems:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"this step cannot enrich with \"\n                                   + (prompt.name or model_id) + \": \"\n                                   + \"; \".join(problems))\n            # Only a prompt whose LLM is a hosted API needs a provider key,\n            # and its own signature is what says so.\n            api_key = \"\"\n            if prompt.needs_api_key:\n                domain = P[\"_rgen_credentialDomain\"] or \"agentic-ai-keys\"\n                secrets = fetch_secrets(BASE, TOKEN, domain, verify=VERIFY) or {}\n                if not secrets:\n                    raise RuntimeError(\n                        \"the enrichment prompt calls a hosted LLM, but no \"\n                        \"credential resolved from domain \" + domain + \" for \"\n                        \"this user - see the Managing Credentials \"\n                        \"administration guide\")\n                api_key = llm_api_key_for(prompt.llm, secrets)\n\n            # A chunk whose vector will be reused was enriched by the run that\n            # embedded it, so calling the LLM again buys a header nobody\n            # stores. Same set the Embed step reuses, read the same way.\n            current_ids = {chunk[\"chunk_id\"] for chunk in chunks}\n            already = {row[\"chunk_id\"]\n                       for row in cas_read(project_table(\"_EMBEDDED\"))\n                       if row.get(\"embedding\") and row.get(\"chunk_id\") in current_ids}\n\n            workers = max(1, int(float(P[\"_rgen_workers\"] or 4)))\n            chunks, failures = run_enrich(chunks, prompt, mapping,\n                                          header_output=header_output,\n                                          column_outputs=column_outputs,\n                                          api_key=api_key, max_workers=workers,\n                                          already_enriched=already, log=M)\n            log_enrich_cost(prompt.llm, prompt.usage, log=M)\n            n_rows = cas_stage(project_table(\"_CHUNKS\"),\n                               [chunk_to_row(chunk) for chunk in chunks],\n                               CHUNK_COLUMNS, numeric=(\"chunk_index\",))\n            # Deliberately NOT stamped into the configuration: enrichment\n            # is not part of the drift fingerprint any more, so changing the\n            # prompt applies from this run onward instead of demanding a full\n            # re-ingest. Each chunk records which prompt wrote it instead.\n            stamp_enrich_usage(inventory, prompt.usage, prompt.llm,\n                               attribute_schema(prompt, column_outputs))\n            n_inventory = write_rows(\"rgen_inventory_out.json\", stamp(inventory),\n                                     inventory_columns, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n            SAS.symput(\"_rgen_nrows\", str(n_rows))\n            SAS.symput(\"_rgen_ninv\", str(n_inventory))\n            summarize(f\"prompt {prompt.name or model_id} \"\n                      f\"(llm {prompt.llm or 'unknown'}, code {prompt.code_hash})\")\n            summarize(f\"{len(chunks) - len(already)} chunks enriched, \"\n                      f\"{len(already)} skipped as already embedded, \"\n                      f\"{len(failures)} failed\")\n            if failures:\n                summarize(\"chunks that failed are embedded WITHOUT a header - \"\n                          f\"first reason: {failures[0][1][:200]}\")\n            if header_output:\n                summarize(f\"'{header_output}' stored as the context header\")\n            if column_outputs:\n                summarize(\"stored as columns: \" + \", \".join(column_outputs))\n            summarize(f\"{n_rows} rows written to \"\n                      f\"{CASLIB}.{project_table('_CHUNKS')}\")\n            publish_summary(\"_rgen_summary\")\n\n        try:\n            conn.close(close_session=False)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgen_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgen_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgen_swap(suffix, count, persist=1);\n    %if &_rgen_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %if &count. LT 0 %then %return;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgencas incaslib=\"&_rgen_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgen_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgen_ragProject.&suffix.\" quiet;\n        %if &count. GT 0 %then %do;\n            promote casdata=\"&_rgen_ragProject.&suffix._S\"\n                    casout=\"&_rgen_ragProject.&suffix.\";\n            %if &persist. EQ 1 %then %do;\n                save casdata=\"&_rgen_ragProject.&suffix.\"\n                     casout=\"&_rgen_ragProject.&suffix.\" replace;\n            %end;\n            %else %do;\n                /* not persisted by choice: clear any file an earlier run\n                   saved, or a restart would resurrect stale content */\n                deletesource casdata=\"&_rgen_ragProject.&suffix..sashdat\" quiet;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n        %else %do;\n            deletesource casdata=\"&_rgen_ragProject.&suffix..sashdat\" quiet;\n        %end;\n    quit;\n%mend _rgen_swap;\n%_rgen_swap(_CHUNKS, &_rgen_nrows., persist=&_rgen_persist.);\n%macro _rgen_passthrough;\n    %if &_rgen_state. NE skip %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgen_invout., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgen_invout., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgenout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgencas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgen_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgen_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if %symexist(_rgen_inventory) %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgen_inventory)) NE 0 %then\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(&_rgen_inventory.)) %then %do;\n        data &_rgen_invout.&opts.;\n            set &_rgen_inventory.;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgen_passthrough;\n%_rgen_passthrough;\n\n%macro _rgen_emit_inventory;\n    %if &_rgen_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgen_invout., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgen_invout., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgenout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgencas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgen_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgen_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if &_rgen_ninv. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rgenino \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgen_inventory_out.json\";\n        libname rgeninj json fileref=rgenino;\n        data &_rgen_invout.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024\n                   embed_usage $ 256 enrich_usage $ 256;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\"\n                  embed_usage=\"Embedding usage (JSON)\"\n                  enrich_usage=\"Enrichment usage (JSON)\";\n            set rgeninj.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rgeninj clear;\n        filename rgenino clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgen_invout.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024\n                   embed_usage $ 256 enrich_usage $ 256;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\"\n                  embed_usage=\"Embedding usage (JSON)\"\n                  enrich_usage=\"Enrichment usage (JSON)\";\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgen_emit_inventory;\n%_rgen_emit_inventory;\n%macro _rgen_release;\n    %local failing;\n    %let failing = 0;\n    %if &_rgen_state. EQ fail %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &_rgen_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgen_rc. NE 0 %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &failing. EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgen_runId) %then %return;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgen_runId)) EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %sysfunc(exist(rgenout.&_rgen_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %return;\n    data rgenout.&_rgen_ragProject._LEDGER_R(replace=yes);\n        set rgenout.&_rgen_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(not (doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"\n                                 and run_id = \"&_rgen_runId.\")));\n    run;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgencas incaslib=\"&_rgen_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgen_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgen_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        promote casdata=\"&_rgen_ragProject._LEDGER_R\"\n                casout=\"&_rgen_ragProject._LEDGER\";\n        save casdata=\"&_rgen_ragProject._LEDGER\"\n             casout=\"&_rgen_ragProject._LEDGER\" replace;\n    quit;\n    data _null_;\n        putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Enrich Chunks: the run lock was released so the run can be retried\";\n    run;\n%mend _rgen_release;\n%_rgen_release;\n\nlibname rgenout clear;\ncas rgencas terminate;\n\n%macro _rgen_status;\n    %if &_rgen_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgen_rc. NE 0 %then\n        %let _rgen_state = fail;\n    %if &_rgen_state. EQ skip %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Enrich Chunks: skipped -----\";\n        run;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    %if &_rgen_state. EQ fail %then %do;\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 1;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"ERROR: RAG - Enrich Chunks failed: %superq(_rgen_error)\";\n        run;\n        %if &RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR. NE 0 %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                abort 42;\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    data _null_;\n        length part $ 500;\n        putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Enrich Chunks -----\";\n        do i = 1 to countw(\"%superq(_rgen_summary)\", \"|\");\n            part = strip(scan(\"%superq(_rgen_summary)\", i, \"|\"));\n            if part ne \"\" then putLog \"NOTE:   \" part;\n        end;\n    run;\n%mend _rgen_status;\n%_rgen_status;"}, "type": "code", "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Calls a manifested prompt from the Prompt Builder once per chunk in <project>_CHUNKS, and writes what it returns back into that table: one output becomes the chunk's context header, which RAG - Embed Chunks prepends before embedding, and any others become their own columns on the chunk table. Leave the prompt model blank to pass chunks through unchanged. Chain the step to run several prompts one after the other; only one of them may write the context header.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_inventory\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"inputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Updated inventory (from RAG - Chunk Documents):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_promptModel\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Model Manager id of the manifested prompt (blank = do not enrich):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_promptVersion\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pin to this Model Manager version id (blank = follow the model):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_mapping\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Prompt input -> chunk field, as input=field;input=field:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"chunk=chunk;document=document\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_headerOutput\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Prompt output stored as the context header (blank = none):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"response\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_columns\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Prompt outputs stored as their own columns, comma separated:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_workers\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"numstepper\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Parallel LLM calls:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"integer\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"min\": 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"max\": null,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"stepsize\": 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_persist\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Chunk table (<project>_CHUNKS) - keep this the same as the Chunk step:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"1\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Save to disk (survives a server restart)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"0\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Keep in memory only (rebuilt on the next run)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_credentialDomain\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Credential domain (holds the provider key when the prompt calls a hosted LLM):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgen_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgen_invout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Updated inventory output (wire this one forward):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - Enrich Chunks step\\n==========\\n\\nThe enrichment slot between chunking and embedding. It calls a prompt you built and evaluated in the Prompt Builder - manifested as a Model Manager model - once for every chunk, and writes what comes back into <project>_CHUNKS: the output you name becomes the chunk's context_header, which RAG - Embed Chunks prepends to the text before embedding, and any other outputs you name are stored as their own columns on the chunk table.\\n\\nThe headline use is contextual chunk headers (\\\"this passage is from the FY2026 policy, section on carry-over\\\"), which is the published remedy for a chunk that reads perfectly in place and means nothing on its own. The same slot classifies a chunk, extracts a date or flags personal data - which of those it does is decided by the prompt, not by this step.\\n\\nThe prompt must have been manifested with the INTEGRATED LLM CALL option, because this step reads its answer; a prompt manifested for the Call LLM node of SAS Intelligent Decisioning returns the request to make rather than making it, and is refused by name. The step executes the prompt's score code in the compute session, exactly as SAS Container Runtime would - so the control over what runs is Model Manager permissions on the prompt project.\\n\\nCost: one LLM call per chunk, every time the corpus is re-chunked. That is usually the largest line in an ingestion, so it is priced in the log while the run is happening and recorded per run in rag_runs (enrich_calls, enrich_input_tokens, enrich_output_tokens, enrich_seconds, enrich_failed) for RAG_RUN_COST. A prompt manifested without the prompt_length and output_length outputs returns no token counts, and its cost then honestly reads as unknown rather than as zero.\\n\\nFailure is per chunk, like everywhere else in this pipeline: a chunk whose call fails, or whose response was not the JSON the prompt asks for, is embedded WITHOUT a header rather than failing the run - and is counted and named in the log, because a collection where a tenth of the chunks have no header retrieves differently from one where all of them do.\\n\\nFlow wiring: chain the document INVENTORY through every step - RAG - List Documents -> Extract Text -> Chunk Documents -> Enrich Chunks -> Embed Chunks -> Load Vector Store. This step reads and rewrites <project>_CHUNKS in place; everything else about the pipeline tables is unchanged. Give every step the SAME project name and caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests, swat and pandas packages.\\n* CAS available; the runner needs write access to the tables caslib.\\n* A prompt manifested from the Prompt Builder with the integrated LLM call, and read access to its Model Manager project.\\n* A credential-domain entry for the LLM's provider, when the prompt calls a hosted API rather than a local container.\\n\\nChanging the prompt, the mapping or the selected outputs changes what a chunk IS, so the configuration fingerprint changes with them and the next run is refused until the pipeline version is bumped. That is deliberate: it forces the re-ingest that makes the collection consistent again.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.0 (02AUG2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgen_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\",\n\t\t\"_rgen_credentialDomain\": \"agentic-ai-keys\",\n\t\t\"_rgen_promptModel\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgen_mapping\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgen_headerOutput\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgen_workers\": 4,\n\t\t\"_rgen_persist\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"1\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Save to disk (survives a server restart)\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgen_columns\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgen_promptVersion\": \"\"\n\t}\n}"}